## This file provide the arguments provided to the VM at startup
## You can find a full list of flags and their behaviours at
## http://erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html

## Name of the node
-name <%= release_name %>@127.0.0.1

## Cookie for distributed erlang
-setcookie <%= release.profile.cookie %>

## Heartbeat management; auto-restarts VM if it dies or becomes unresponsive
## (Disabled by default..use with caution!)
-heart

## Enable kernel poll for better I/O performance (epoll on Linux, kqueue on BSD/macOS)
+K true

## Dirty I/O schedulers - handles file and network I/O operations
## Default is 10, increase for heavy I/O workloads (database, HTTP, NATS)
+SDio 32

## Increase number of concurrent ports/sockets
## Needed for: database connection pools, HTTP connections, NATS connections
+Q 65536

## Disable busy waiting to reduce CPU usage in containers
## Schedulers won't spin-wait when idle, reducing CPU consumption
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none

## Increase process limit (default 262144)
## Blockscout spawns many processes for concurrent fetching
+P 1000000

## Increase atom limit (default 1048576)
## Large codebases with many modules can exhaust atoms
+t 2000000

# Enable SMP automatically based on availability
# On OTP21+, this is not needed anymore.
-smp auto
